# Agent instructions vendored in by tooling, not authored here.
#
# `shadcn` pulls `.agents/skills/frontend-design/` from `anthropics/skills` and
# records it in `skills-lock.json`. It is not committed, for the same reason
# `agentRules: false` is set in `next.config.ts`: this repository's agent
# instructions are `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` at the root, and a second set
# further down the tree competes with them.
#
# In this case it also *contradicts* one — the skill asks for a distinctive
# visual identity and "one real aesthetic risk", while `docs/console.md §8` says
# shadcn/ui defaults until there is something to be consistent with. Re-created
# by the tool on demand if anybody wants to read it.
/.agents/
/skills-lock.json
